{"cells": [{"cell_type": "markdown", "id": "b6bb9a1f", "metadata": {}, "source": ["# Patent Atypicality (z-scores) \u2014 CPC-subclass pairs, hypergeometric (Youn-style) null\n", "\n", "For each US utility patent, atypicality is measured from the pairs of **its own CPC subclasses** using an\n", "**analytic hypergeometric null** evaluated on the **cumulative** patent set up to the patent's grant year\n", "(Youn et al. 2015 style). Primary key: `patent_id`.\n", "\n", "## Raw data (directory & structure)\n", "```\n", "E:/Dawoon Jeong/Data/PatentView/Granted/g_cpc_current.tsv.zip   # patent_id, cpc_subclass, cpc_type -> a patent's own CPC subclasses\n", "Data/Patent_Metrics/patent_all_metrics_with_disruption.parquet  # patent_id, grant_year\n", "```\n", "A patent contributes the set of its distinct **inventional** CPC subclasses (patents with \u2265 2 subclasses).\n", "\n", "## Metric (formula)\n", "Let $P(t)$ be the cumulative set of patents up to grant year $t$; for a subclass pair $(\\alpha,\\beta)$ let\n", "$n_\\alpha,n_\\beta$ be the cumulative number of patents carrying each subclass, $N=|P(t)|$, and\n", "$o_{\\alpha\\beta}$ the cumulative co-occurrence count. The hypergeometric null gives\n", "$$\\mu_{\\alpha\\beta}=\\frac{n_\\alpha n_\\beta}{N},\\qquad\n", "\\sigma^2_{\\alpha\\beta}=\\mu_{\\alpha\\beta}\\Bigl(1-\\tfrac{n_\\alpha}{N}\\Bigr)\\Bigl(\\tfrac{N-n_\\beta}{N-1}\\Bigr),\\qquad\n", "z_{\\alpha\\beta}=\\frac{o_{\\alpha\\beta}-\\mu_{\\alpha\\beta}}{\\sigma_{\\alpha\\beta}}.$$\n", "$z<0$ = atypical (two common subclasses co-occurring less than chance). Per patent we report the\n", "**median**, **10th percentile**, and **min** of its pairs' $z$ (the min is the most atypical pairing).\n", "\n", "## Output (two files)\n", "- `notebook/patent/output/patent_z_score.parquet` \u2014 `patent_id, Z_median, Z_10pct, Z_min, n_pairs`.\n", "- `notebook/patent/output/z_score_pair.parquet` \u2014 `code_1, code_2, year, Z_score` (per CPC-subclass-pair\n", "  per year, evaluated on the cumulative null at that year).\n", "\n", "> Fast (~a few minutes; analytic null, no shuffling). Column names are generic (`Z_*`); the *method* is\n", "> the Youn-style hypergeometric null. `tqdm` shows a per-year progress bar."]}, {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": 2, "id": "d24099d9-3daa-4dbc-9b3d-365f34652487", "metadata": {}, "outputs": [{"data": {"text/html": ["<div>\n", "<style scoped>\n", "    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n", "        vertical-align: middle;\n", "    }\n", "\n", "    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n", "        vertical-align: top;\n", "    }\n", "\n", "    .dataframe thead th {\n", "        text-align: right;\n", "    }\n", "</style>\n", "<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n", "  <thead>\n", "    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n", "      <th></th>\n", "      <th>work_id</th>\n", "      <th>work_year</th>\n", "      <th>work_id_source_id</th>\n", "      <th>referenced_work_id</th>\n", "      <th>referenced_work_year</th>\n", "      <th>referenced_work_id_source_id</th>\n", "    </tr>\n", "  </thead>\n", "  <tbody>\n", "    <tr>\n", "      <th>0</th>\n", "      <td>W2142411926</td>\n", "      <td>2004.0</td>\n", "      <td>None</td>\n", "      <td>W2107080958</td>\n", "      <td>1998.0</td>\n", "      <td>S90422530</td>\n", "    </tr>\n", "    <tr>\n", "      <th>1</th>\n", "      <td>W2142411926</td>\n", "      <td>2004.0</td>\n", "      <td>None</td>\n", "      <td>W1861501842</td>\n", "      <td>2002.0</td>\n", "      <td>None</td>\n", "    </tr>\n", "    <tr>\n", "      <th>2</th>\n", "      <td>W1976340576</td>\n", "      <td>2004.0</td>\n", "      <td>S54553633</td>\n", "      <td>W1966155544</td>\n", "      <td>1994.0</td>\n", "      <td>S24807848</td>\n", "    </tr>\n", "    <tr>\n", "      <th>3</th>\n", "      <td>W1976340576</td>\n", "      <td>2004.0</td>\n", "      <td>S54553633</td>\n", "      <td>W1976363242</td>\n", "      <td>1997.0</td>\n", "      <td>S186881120</td>\n", "    </tr>\n", "    <tr>\n", "      <th>4</th>\n", "      <td>W1976340576</td>\n", "      <td>2004.0</td>\n", "      <td>S54553633</td>\n", "      <td>W2017774710</td>\n", "      <td>1999.0</td>\n", "      <td>S4210224030</td>\n", "    </tr>\n", "  </tbody>\n", "</table>\n", "</div>"], "text/plain": ["       work_id  work_year work_id_source_id referenced_work_id  \\\n", "0  W2142411926     2004.0              None        W2107080958   \n", "1  W2142411926     2004.0              None        W1861501842   \n", "2  W1976340576     2004.0         S54553633        W1966155544   \n", "3  W1976340576     2004.0         S54553633        W1976363242   \n", "4  W1976340576     2004.0         S54553633        W2017774710   \n", "\n", "   referenced_work_year referenced_work_id_source_id  \n", "0                1998.0                    S90422530  \n", "1                2002.0                         None  \n", "2                1994.0                    S24807848  \n", "3                1997.0                   S186881120  \n", "4                1999.0                  S4210224030  "]}, "execution_count": 2, "metadata": {}, "output_type": "execute_result"}], "source": ["import pandas as pd\n", "temp_df = pd.read_parquet('/project/jevans/Dawoon/Science of Science/OpenAlex/output/referenced_works_w_year/part_1329.parquet')\n", "temp_df.head()"]}, {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": 1, "id": "5739c922", "metadata": {"execution": {"iopub.execute_input": "2026-08-26T21:53:03.861372Z", "iopub.status.busy": "2026-08-26T21:53:03.861372Z", "iopub.status.idle": "2026-08-26T21:53:04.127174Z", "shell.execute_reply": "2026-08-26T21:53:04.127174Z"}}, "outputs": [{"name": "stdout", "output_type": "stream", "text": ["ROOT: C:\\Users\\jdwoo\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\Research\\Science of Science\n"]}], "source": ["# Imports these cells use but never declared -- they were carried in from an\n", "# earlier kernel session, so the notebook only ran interactively.\n", "from tqdm.auto import tqdm\n", "from collections import defaultdict\n", "from itertools import combinations\n", "from math import sqrt\n", "import os, sys, gc, time\n", "import numpy as np, pandas as pd\n", "sys.path.insert(0, '/project/jevans/Dawoon/Science of Science/PatentView')\n", "import pv_common as pv\n", "ROOT, D, OUT = pv.BASE, pv.GRANTED, pv.OUT\n", "OUT_FP = pv.out('patent_z_score.parquet')\n", "# The Windows layout read grant years from Data/Patent_Metrics/patent_all_metrics_with_\n", "# disruption.parquet, which does not exist here. patent_metadata.parquet carries the same\n", "# column, so this notebook now depends on patent_metadata having been run first.\n", "PM_META = pv.out('patent_metadata.parquet')\n", "pv.preflight('patent_z_score')"]}, {"cell_type": "markdown", "id": "7d7188c3", "metadata": {}, "source": ["## 1. Build inputs: grant years + each patent's own CPC subclasses (>= 2)"]}, {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": 2, "id": "17f92821", "metadata": {"execution": {"iopub.execute_input": "2026-08-26T21:53:04.128178Z", "iopub.status.busy": "2026-08-26T21:53:04.128178Z", "iopub.status.idle": "2026-08-26T21:54:36.006160Z", "shell.execute_reply": "2026-08-26T21:54:36.006160Z"}}, "outputs": [{"name": "stdout", "output_type": "stream", "text": ["patents with >=2 CPC subclasses: 4,160,856\n", "CPU times: total: 1min 30s\n", "Wall time: 1min 31s\n"]}], "source": ["%%time\n", "meta = pd.read_parquet(PM_META, columns=['patent_id', 'grant_year'])\n", "meta['patent_id'] = meta['patent_id'].astype(str)\n", "year_of = dict(zip(meta['patent_id'], meta['grant_year'].astype(int))); del meta\n", "\n", "cpc = pd.read_csv(os.path.join(D, 'g_cpc_current.tsv.zip'), sep='\\t',\n", "                  usecols=['patent_id', 'cpc_subclass', 'cpc_type'],\n", "                  dtype={'patent_id': str, 'cpc_subclass': str, 'cpc_type': str})\n", "cpc = cpc[(cpc['cpc_type'] == 'inventional')].dropna(subset=['cpc_subclass'])\n", "cpc = cpc[cpc['patent_id'].isin(year_of)]\n", "code_set = {}\n", "for pid, grp in cpc.groupby('patent_id')['cpc_subclass']:\n", "    s = sorted(set(grp))\n", "    if len(s) >= 2:\n", "        code_set[pid] = s\n", "del cpc; gc.collect()\n", "print(f'patents with >=2 CPC subclasses: {len(code_set):,}')"]}, {"cell_type": "markdown", "id": "2517f12b", "metadata": {}, "source": ["## 2. Cumulative hypergeometric (Youn-style) z-scores"]}, {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": 3, "id": "c15263b2", "metadata": {"execution": {"iopub.execute_input": "2026-08-26T21:54:36.007672Z", "iopub.status.busy": "2026-08-26T21:54:36.007672Z", "iopub.status.idle": "2026-08-26T21:57:44.005546Z", "shell.execute_reply": "2026-08-26T21:57:44.005546Z"}}, "outputs": [{"name": "stderr", "output_type": "stream", "text": ["\r", "atypicality by year (cumulative):   0%|          | 0/50 [00:00<?, ?it/s]"]}, {"name": "stderr", "output_type": "stream", "text": ["\r", "atypicality by year (cumulative):   2%|\u258f         | 1/50 [00:01<01:03,  1.29s/it]"]}, {"name": "stderr", "output_type": "stream", "text": ["\r", "atypicality by year (cumulative):   4%|\u258d         | 2/50 [00:02<00:54,  1.15s/it]"]}, {"name": "stderr", "output_type": "stream", "text": ["\r", "atypicality by year (cumulative):   6%|\u258c         | 3/50 [00:03<00:50,  1.07s/it]"]}, {"name": "stderr", "output_type": "stream", "text": ["\r", "atypicality by year (cumulative):   8%|\u258a         | 4/50 [00:04<00:43,  1.06it/s]"]}, {"name": "stderr", "output_type": "stream", "text": ["\r", "atypicality by year (cumulative):  10%|\u2588         | 5/50 [00:05<00:43,  1.03it/s]"]}, {"name": "stderr", "output_type": "stream", "text": ["\r", "atypicality by year (cumulative):  12%|\u2588\u258f        | 6/50 [00:06<00:44,  1.02s/it]"]}, {"name": "stderr", "output_type": "stream", "text": ["\r", "atypicality by year (cumulative):  14%|\u2588\u258d        | 7/50 [00:07<00:43,  1.01s/it]"]}, {"name": "stderr", "output_type": "stream", "text": ["\r", "atypicality by year (cumulative):  16%|\u2588\u258c        | 8/50 [00:08<00:42,  1.02s/